#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105464 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6c58537-344e-5842-b68c-d9b5a9d7ca96" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "fc5fc31e-f585-5d15-8a8a-eb0d19704e9a" :question/math-academy-id "e-2947" :question/problem "Find the area of the triangle $\\triangle ABC$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1397/Source/Images/3b4d9c9c491ffbfc0029c8dc8fbdec5f.png)" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = \\dfrac{b \\cdot h}{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nb &= AB \\\\\n&= AH + HB \\\\\n&= 6 + 3 \\\\\n&= 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding height is\n$h={CH} = 4$.\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{b \\cdot h}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9 \\cdot 4}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{36}{2} \\\\\n&= 18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105465 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6445834c-7788-5427-a72c-30b06cc8e6ab" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of an Isosceles Right Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "cdb1d145-6e8a-5213-a7f7-8076440cbbeb" :question/math-academy-id "e-2949" :question/problem "What is the area of the right triangle $ABC$ shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1397/Source/Images/6e33b27de00dd277467a671bfd437fe1.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since\n\n$$\nm\\angle{A}=m\\angle{C}\n$$\n\nwe have an isosceles triangle, where $AB=BC$.\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{1}{2}AB \\cdot BC \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 8 \\cdot 8 \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 8^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 64 \\\\\n&= 32\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105466 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Base or the Height of a Triangle Given Its Area"}] :question/id #uuid "58e1ce31-f6fc-5900-ab89-e00241045b12" :question/math-academy-id "e-2950" :question/problem "Consider the triangles $\\triangle ABC$ and $\\triangle CDE$ shown below. If the area of $\\triangle CDE$ is $25 \\textrm{cm}^2$, find the area of $\\triangle ABC$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1397/Source/Images/da9f32aef805e352321a281de43fe6ef.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider $\\triangle CDE$. We can see that $\\overline{CD}$ is the height corresponding to the base $\\overline{DE}$ and that\n\n$$\nDE=10\\textrm{cm}\n$$\n\nSince the area of $\\triangle CDE$ is $25\\textrm{cm}^2$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{b \\cdot h}{2} \\\\\n25 &= \\frac{10 \\cdot CD}{2} \\\\\n25 &= 5 \\cdot CD \\\\\nCD &= 5cm\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that $\\overline{CD}$ is also the height of $\\triangle ABC$ corresponding to the base $\\overline{AB}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1397/Source/Images/007cd77422021914a9dee871680fdecb.png)\n\nTherefore, we find the area of $\\triangle ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{b \\cdot h}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{AB \\cdot CD}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{6 \\cdot 5}{2} \\\\\n&= 15cm^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252324 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6c58537-344e-5842-b68c-d9b5a9d7ca96" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b644fba2-8695-52af-a5f2-f12feb6c8041" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252326} {:answer/id #uuid "5ef215a6-dd7f-5c76-af76-09559e17828c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "47" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252327} {:answer/id #uuid "0505e69b-b92a-57a9-90ad-38b13e31834d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252328} {:answer/id #uuid "1ebc4df5-ec54-5260-be2a-a75f29648f35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252329} {:answer/id #uuid "b17ee8df-2108-55cf-b502-0546f5f809b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0505e69b-b92a-57a9-90ad-38b13e31834d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252328} :answer-field/id #uuid "fad3d47f-4a17-5aac-9569-63a84d8dbf0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252325}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4c8383ab-8434-5054-a648-180814c70091" :question/math-academy-id "q-117335" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945897/assets/3989bb27499cb1d20740ab347a1205d2c75c85c894829db054906a3bf5eb18ed.png)\n\nFind the area of the triangle $△ABC.$\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)" :question/worked-solution "The area of the triangle is defined as \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =AB \\\\  & =AH+HB \\\\  & =11+5 \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding height is\n\n$$\nh=CH=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\cdot 7}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{112}{2} \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252331 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6445834c-7788-5427-a72c-30b06cc8e6ab" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of an Isosceles Right Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83895312-ad54-52cc-bcb2-e6dec3a7ef4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "113" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252333} {:answer/id #uuid "e800af70-4bd9-59f4-9c3b-ec78d33b73a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252334} {:answer/id #uuid "626fda71-308e-5c59-a0b5-33c5a6fc85c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252335} {:answer/id #uuid "544d5d94-7f13-59c0-9c05-fefcf0c225a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "84.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252336} {:answer/id #uuid "8a144769-30ee-5e5f-82fc-bac2fc4eb7bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "169" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "544d5d94-7f13-59c0-9c05-fefcf0c225a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "84.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252336} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c084c2a-7890-5b0b-a8cf-8ef7a9a06a17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252332}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b82680f-f801-5d98-98f5-3b30c67dd0ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-117347" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945897/assets/4aa952124ddaaa1dc2a54ebb4601255ae42346a9e02f02391c05453a81542505.png)\n\nWhat is the area of the right triangle $ABC$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Since $m∠A=m∠C={45}^{∘}$ and $AB=BC,$ we have an isosceles right triangle. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945897/assets/670afdec3633984b2fb493706e762740062348ccbdd0f56df14e3add3d4bbd23.png)\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {13}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 169 \\\\  & =84.5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252338 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Base or the Height of a Triangle Given Its Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74a6c9f1-77c5-5dc0-9464-9cd29fe23947" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252340} {:answer/id #uuid "e95b7857-a2b3-528c-b0ac-5577c1ee1d1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252341} {:answer/id #uuid "d012c751-ac5d-5125-b9b6-cda3e0d86790" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252342} {:answer/id #uuid "f8248279-d0d8-5cc9-b109-d775eb59db85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252343} {:answer/id #uuid "b750770d-28f8-5052-a46b-9c91524753ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d012c751-ac5d-5125-b9b6-cda3e0d86790" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252342} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5043b17-ebe0-57ee-80ec-5aab94ccabec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252339}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4303d1bd-0440-58eb-a5d5-e6551f7a6e46" :question/math-academy-id "q-117356" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945897/assets/10b6f63df56c789d0d28cd14caad0a2588e247ba4a60239f4cb0dd5a32777daf.png)\n\nFind $AM$ given that the area of $△ABC$ is $64\\,{m}^{2},$ $MC=11\\,m,$ and $BM=8\\,m.$}\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)" :question/worked-solution "The area of the triangle is defined as \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is $b=AC,$ and the corresponding height is \n\n$$\nh=BM=8\\,m.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the formula for the area, we can solve for the base as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 64 & =\\frac{b\\cdot 8}{2} \\\\ 128 & =b\\cdot 8 \\\\ b & =\\frac{128}{8} \\\\ b & =16\\,m\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $AC=16\\,m$ and hence, we have\n\n$$\nAM=AC-MC=16-11=5\\,\\text{m}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252345 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Base or the Height of a Triangle Given Its Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "048d8d61-7908-5cf0-8096-82fd4425c783" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252347} {:answer/id #uuid "e6accb97-5480-52e9-931b-b2880998af09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17.5{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252348} {:answer/id #uuid "f67e787d-757a-50dd-90e9-7c10c9a1f995" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252349} {:answer/id #uuid "2c092507-9ec5-5d2c-bcb4-98b045e089a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.5{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252350} {:answer/id #uuid "d5bb2628-1bb2-5b4f-a5a0-8b3dbf59f09a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6accb97-5480-52e9-931b-b2880998af09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17.5{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252348} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f73c6ce-729a-571b-a4f2-a88cabcb062d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252346}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c457037c-f30c-55b6-9f52-d739e0d113b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-117365" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945897/assets/4310195e821f7c09399073a2b4eb3e10c262ad61cbb3fe8d951645caee51a4d0.png)\n\nConsider the triangles $△ABC$ and $△BCD$ shown above. If the area of $△BCD$ is $42{\\text{ in}}^{2}$, find the area of $△ABC.$\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider $△BCD.$ We can see that $\\overset{―}{BC}$ is the height corresponding to the base $\\overset{―}{CD}$ and that $CD=12\\text{ in}.$ \n\nSince the area of $△BCD$ is $42{\\text{ in}}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 42 & =\\frac{CD\\cdot BC}{2} \\\\ 42 & =\\frac{12\\cdot BC}{2} \\\\ 84 & =12\\cdot BC \\\\ BC & =\\frac{84}{12} \\\\ BC & =7\\text{ in}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that $\\overset{―}{BC}$ is also the height of $△ABC$ corresponding to the base $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Therefore, we find the area of $△ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{AB\\cdot BC}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 7}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{2} \\\\  & =17.5{\\text{ in}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252352 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Base or the Height of a Triangle Given Its Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "742e1daa-d481-5df7-9ca6-9b2b1c89b36c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252354} {:answer/id #uuid "568854ca-c43b-5d15-befc-8d1ffe985593" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252355} {:answer/id #uuid "7f89799e-4e6c-5dfc-a5a8-85b394aefb0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252356} {:answer/id #uuid "3bbd7008-9c99-5dec-90b3-74724de488d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252357} {:answer/id #uuid "65367e9d-4ee2-5f36-851c-39758476675e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "568854ca-c43b-5d15-befc-8d1ffe985593" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252355} :answer-field/id #uuid "a450a329-d5cd-527f-9d2f-b92ac44d1261" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252353}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8450a28f-9fa7-54f9-a61c-39e7c40a3f14" :question/math-academy-id "q-117374" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945897/assets/45d1ad7a8cf54a09c2605e2afd3af415de4e42726923bf4771af79aa66079f05.png)\n\nFind $AB$ given that the area of $△ABC$ is $140\\,{m}^{2}$ and $CH=14\\,m.$\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is a base and $h$ the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is $b=AB,$ and the corresponding height is \n\n$$\nh=CH=14\\,m.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the formula for the area, we can solve for the base as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 140 & =\\frac{b\\cdot 14}{2} \\\\ 280 & =b\\cdot 14 \\\\ b & =\\frac{280}{14} \\\\ b & =20\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $AB=20\\,\\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252359 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6c58537-344e-5842-b68c-d9b5a9d7ca96" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f34bbb67-6b98-5e29-90e1-946e52cfcafa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f34bbb67-6b98-5e29-90e1-946e52cfcafa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252361} :answer-field/id #uuid "080bfc84-6393-5dcd-9e1c-b00410b2e1d0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252360}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e06b4ab-b9c5-5449-8956-0940025463f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-171955" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945897/assets/eb2cfa5b66dc7e1214dac646d6d21c573385c72fe71d5194b6716824b0258cca.png)\n\nThe area of the triangle $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}.\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)" :question/worked-solution "The area of the triangle is defined as \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =AB \\\\  & =AH+HB \\\\  & =6+4 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding height is\n\n$$\nh=CH=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\cdot 6}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{60}{2} \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Base or the Height of a Triangle Given Its Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4a3b44b-f034-50b3-b0e3-300e2ba46a56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18cm^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104412} {:answer/id #uuid "de0ab294-9c50-55c3-a021-e4e6516dde36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10cm^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104413} {:answer/id #uuid "21021f18-c033-581d-bccf-251b62f93963" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12cm^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104414} {:answer/id #uuid "32cbcf3e-90b9-5ea0-b4b2-65cd71eb120e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32cm^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104415} {:answer/id #uuid "5e8d785c-5136-5419-b2c5-e8b96665e69c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24cm^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21021f18-c033-581d-bccf-251b62f93963" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12cm^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104414} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ccf8bec-203f-57e2-9b45-65287d0941e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104411}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c9de4737-5690-569a-aafc-7e16a64e500e" :question/math-academy-id "q-52865" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1397/Source/Images/q-52865.png)\n\nConsider the triangles $△ABC$ and $△CDE$ shown above. If the area of $△CDE$ is $18cm^{2}$, find the area of $△ABC$." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider $△CDE.$ We can see that $\\overset{―}{CD}$ is the height corresponding to the base $\\overset{―}{DE}$ and that $DE=6\\text{ cm}.$ \n\nSince the area of $△CDE$ is $18{\\text{ cm}}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 18 & =\\frac{6\\cdot CD}{2} \\\\ 3CD & =18 \\\\ CD & =6\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that $\\overset{―}{CD}$ is also the height of $△ABC$ corresponding to the base $\\overset{―}{AB}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945897/assets/87c774cbdce6c4858605e2b8c6186abc6dde73b2b636966b4049ded4f82af684.png)\n\nTherefore, we find the area of $△ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{AB\\cdot CD}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 6}{2} \\\\  & =12{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "